    "notes": "UH-68 Heron, a utility transport analogue of the UH-60A Black Hawk. Figures from NASA CR-166309 (Howlett, GenHel), NASA TM-85890 and Army manuals as quoted in public sources: rotor geometry, speed, hinge offset, engines, transmission, inertias, flat-plate area, tail rotor cant. Twist is the nonlinear -18 deg as linear -16; hub stiffness from a 0.381 m hinge offset and 115 kg blades; drag areas off the x axis and tail surfaces are tuning values. Model frame: x forward, y up, z starboard, origin on the ground under the main rotor shaft; the model's hub stands at 4.0 m (the real 3.76 m), so the CG is 1.7 m under it.",
